okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Session backup on a full disk / a huge work folder: stop instead of silently skipping, check space first, show progress with cancel, choose excluded folders and the file limit in the menu, never crash the menu."
reported: "User, 2026-10-10: 500 '[Errno 28] No space left on device' writing oauth-tokens.state.json ('디스크 스페이는 많은데?'); a menu backup crashed with OSError 28 in record_state; 'G:\\ciel-Walkie에서 다시백업했으나 백업종료후 멈춤'; '지금 아무것도 안움직이고 프리즈상태라고'; then '저위에 있는 미결된 두가지사항 마져 처리해'."
diagnosis:
  disk: "C: SizeRemaining 0 (Get-Volume). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Temp 150 GB, of which Temp\\claude\\G--ciel-Walkie 114 GB: the scratchpad of Claude session 417ef30b holds 161 wt-* folders (95 GB, each with node_modules/electron); 133 of the 168 git worktrees of G:\\ciel-Walkie point there. Not cleaned: another project's work, waiting for the user's choice. The session backup target was 0.06 GB - not the cause."
  freeze: "Menu pid 99508 was waiting on 'backup create --cwd G:\\ciel-Walkie' (pid 106988) with no progress output and a 15-minute limit; the child kept reading (4.9 GB read, CPU rising) but every chunk write failed with ENOSPC and was skipped per file; the work folder is ~173 GB (.local 144 GB, .claude 19.7 GB, release 7.5 GB). The child was stopped (it had stored nothing); the menu returned."
changes:
  target_errors: "session_backup_store.TargetWriteError: a chunk write/has failure on a target (ENOSPC flagged as 'no space left on the target') stops the whole backup; per-file read errors are still skipped and listed."
  preflight: "session_backup_cli.preflight: for local targets the work folder is measured (same excludes, same file limit) and compared with the target's free space; a first backup that cannot fit, or <256 MB free, is refused before reading, naming the largest folders and what to do."
  progress_cancel: "backup create --progress-file (files, read, stored; 'measuring' phase); session_backup_service.run_backup uses Popen, polls progress, on_progress can cancel, no time limit by default (the restart/session-end trigger keeps 600 s and prints progress); the reason is always recorded ('cancelled', the child's JSON error, or the exit code); state writes never raise; MCP create starts in the background and status shows progress."
  menu: "Back up now shows one in-place progress line (console width) with Esc to cancel; failure reasons wrapped onto several lines; new rows 'Exclude from the work folder…' (lists the largest entries with sizes, up to 20 s, then edits per-workspace patterns used by every backup) and 'Largest single file to back up [1024 MB]'; the result lists files left out ('Not in this backup: N file(s) … e.g. cwd/src/huge-model.bin: 1100 MB, over the 1024 MB file limit'); any panel error becomes a message instead of closing the menu."
tests: "tests/test_session_backup.py 39 (new: full target stops the backup, preflight refuses/permits, menu excludes used by the next backup, menu errors as messages, cancel keeps the reason, failure without output has a reason, child JSON error is the reason); CLI tests pin disk_usage so the host disk does not decide them. Groups: unit 1803 OK, runtime 399 OK, router 1188 OK; channel: test_channel_transcript_repository fails here on this PC on the current tree and on committed HEAD (2 of 3 runs) - environment, not investigated. ruff clean."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_backup_safety.py (+ _steps.py, console_driver.py): scratch on G: (C: had 230-570 MB free), isolated config, menu in conhost driven by key events. Work folder: bigdata/ 12 x 256 MB, src/main.py, src/huge-model.bin 1100 MB. Targets: cdrive (a folder on C:) and built-in local (G:)."
  result: "Run 2026-10-10 13:04: 'Backup not saved: not enough space on target cdrive (...): 570 MB free, the work folder is 3.0 GB for a first backup (largest: bigdata 3.0 GB, src 0 MB). Exclude big folders ... or choose a target with more room.' and nothing written to C:; with local: 'Backing up: 1 files, 89.0 MB read, 88.0 MB stored (4 s)  Esc cancels' then Esc -> 'Backup not saved: cancelled'; Exclude row listed 'bigdata 3072.0 MB, src 0.0 MB' and saved 'bigdata'; Back up now -> saved, incremental line, 'Not in this backup: 1 file(s) ... cwd/src/huge-model.bin: 1100 MB, over the 1024 MB file limit'; snapshot cwd files ['src/main.py']."
not_verified:
  - "A real multi-hour backup of G:\\ciel-Walkie to G:\\backup\\andy (not run)."
  - "SSH/S3/rclone targets running out of space (TargetWriteError covers OSError from them; not exercised)."
not_done: "Not committed/pushed/deployed. C: cleanup of the Walkie worktrees awaits the user's choice."
